@*
    FULL MENU OFFCANVAS (phone + tablet). Lifted out of MainLayout unchanged.
    Opened from the MoreSheet "Full menu" button and the NavRail menu button, both of
    which target #mobileSidebar through Bootstrap's offcanvas data-api, so the DOM here
    (ids, classes, data-bs-* attributes, links, icons and their order) must stay exactly
    as MainLayout used to render it.

    WHY IT IS ITS OWN COMPONENT
    This subtree is ~1,000 lines and holds ~50 NavLink components, yet it changes only
    when the user toggles one of its submenus or when the signed-in user's permissions
    change. It deliberately declares NO parameters: Blazor only calls SetParametersAsync
    on a retained child component when its parameter view may have changed, and an empty
    parameter view never changes, so every MainLayout re-render (More sheet, user menu,
    toast, session dialog, search keystroke, navigation) now skips this whole tree.
    Everything it needs is injected, and it re-renders itself from LoginState.OnChange.
    Active-link highlighting needs no work here: NavLink subscribes to
    NavigationManager.LocationChanged on its own.
*@

<div class="offcanvas offcanvas-start"
     tabindex="-1"
     id="mobileSidebar"
     aria-labelledby="mobileSidebarLabel">

    <div class="offcanvas-header">

        <h5 class="offcanvas-title brand p-0 m-0"
            id="mobileSidebarLabel"
            style="font-size:1.6rem;">

            SPIC

        </h5>

        <button type="button"
                class="btn-close"
                data-bs-dismiss="offcanvas"
                aria-label="Close">
        </button>

    </div>


    <div class="offcanvas-body">

        <nav class="nav nav-pills flex-column nav-section">

